            <p>Vertebral Artery Injury.&#x000a0;High-risk imaging patterns prompting CTA screening for blunt vertebral artery injury (VAI). Representative CT images show a cervical fracture with subluxation (CT sagittal reconstruction, upper right) and a fracture involving the transverse foramen (CT axial bone window, lower right). CT angiography (CTA) demonstrates unilateral vertebral artery occlusion (red arrow) with a patent contralateral vertebral artery (blue arrow) (axial CTA, lower left). Abbreviations: CT, computed tomography; VA, vertebral artery. Contributed by K Margetis, MD</p>
